{"units":[
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity.go:ParseQuantity","summary":"ParseQuantity now calls CacheString on the Quantity it builds in the int64 fast path and the inf.Dec path, so the canonical string is stored at parse time. This moves the string computation (and its allocation) into every parse and relies on String no longer caching.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"ParseQuantity now eagerly caches the canonical string","confidence":0.85,"reason":"Changes what every parsed Quantity holds (q.s) and shifts cost and caching semantics for a widely used public parser.","risk_signals":["public API behavior","performance of hot parse path","unexported field populated differently (affects DeepEqual)"],"focus":["every return path of ParseQuantity sets s (including the fast path that reuses the input string)","extra allocation cost on parse-heavy paths","callers or tests comparing Quantity with reflect.DeepEqual"]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity.go:(*Quantity).String","summary":"String no longer writes the computed string back into the receiver; it returns the cached value if present or recomputes it each call. This removes a data race on concurrent String calls but makes String on non-parsed Quantities recompute every time.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Quantity.String no longer mutates receiver or caches result","confidence":0.85,"reason":"Alters caching and mutation semantics of a core method used in encoding, with performance and concurrency consequences.","risk_signals":["concurrency semantics","performance regression for quantities built without ParseQuantity","public API behavior"],"focus":["hot callers that build Quantity via NewQuantity/MustParse alternatives and call String repeatedly","code relying on String populating q.s (DeepEqual comparisons)","encoding paths (JSON, proto) that call String more than once"]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity.go:(*Quantity).CacheString","summary":"Adds a new exported method that computes the canonical string and always stores it in the receiver. It is meant for callers who own the instance, and is used by ParseQuantity.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Add exported Quantity.CacheString that stores canonical string","confidence":0.8,"reason":"New public API that mutates the receiver and is on the ParseQuantity path.","risk_signals":["new public API","mutates receiver"],"focus":["unconditional write to q.s is a race if called on a shared instance","stale q.s is returned unchanged if a quantity was mutated without clearing s"]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity_test.go:TestQuantityString","summary":"The test now expects ParseQuantity to have set the cached string, instead of expecting it empty after parse and set by String. The expectation was changed to match the new behavior.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"test","headline":"TestQuantityString now expects string cached at parse time","confidence":0.7,"reason":"An expectation was changed to match new behavior and an assertion was removed, which could hide a regression.","risk_signals":["expectation changed to match new behavior","assertion removed"],"focus":["that the removed check (String populates q.s) is intentionally dropped","that the new assertion q.s == item.expect covers all table entries"]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity_test.go:TestQuantityCacheString","summary":"New test checking that CacheString returns and stores the canonical string, is idempotent, and handles nil. Only adds coverage.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Add test for Quantity.CacheString","confidence":0.92,"reason":"New test only; cannot affect production behavior.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity_test.go:BenchmarkQuantityString","summary":"Benchmark rewritten to use sub-benchmarks per quantity with b.Loop, and the Precalc variant was removed. Benchmark-only change.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Rewrite String benchmark as per-case sub-benchmarks","confidence":0.9,"reason":"Benchmark-only; no production code affected.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity_test.go:BenchmarkQuantityStringBinarySI","summary":"Benchmark rewritten into sub-benchmarks using b.Loop. Benchmark-only change.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Rewrite BinarySI String benchmark as sub-benchmarks","confidence":0.9,"reason":"Benchmark-only; no production code affected.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
